From: EmpiierOS Trusted Substrate
Subject: [PATCH] systemd.mk: use grep -E instead of egrep

Fedora's /usr/bin/egrep is a wrapper that prints an obsolescence
warning on every invoke. Buildroot's getty console install rule used
egrep -q; replace with grep -E -q so finalize stays silent.


--- a/package/systemd/systemd.mk
+++ b/package/systemd/systemd.mk
@@ -772 +772 @@ define SYSTEMD_INSTALL_SERVICE_TTY
-	elif echo $(BR2_TARGET_GENERIC_GETTY_PORT) | egrep -q 'tty[0-9]*$$'; \
+	elif echo $(BR2_TARGET_GENERIC_GETTY_PORT) | grep -E -q 'tty[0-9]*$$'; \
